 LT.lt.{u_1} x1 x2] →\n                motive ⋯) →\n              motive t","unsafe":false,"value":174,"source":{"code":"/-- Typeclass for strict reverse monotonicity of multiplication by nonnegative elements on\nthe left, namely `b * a₁ < b * a₂ → a₁ < a₂` if `0 ≤ b`.\n\nYou should usually not use this very granular typeclass directly, but rather a typeclass like\n`LinearOrderedSemiring`. -/\n@[mk_iff] class PosMulReflectLT : Prop extends ContravariantClass α≥0 α (fun x y => x * y) (· < ·)","start":112,"end":117},"axioms":[]}